Chapter 10: “The Lion King’s Land”
Chapter 10, Section 22: “Preparations and Refusal”

――This scene took place in the commercial district of the Royal Capital of Lugunica, at the very same time that Natsuki Subaru, in the hideout of the “Six Tongues,” was being informed of the colossal danger threatening the Kingdom of Lugunica.

“――By some means or another, the enemy has already gotten their hands on the Dragon History Stone and seized full authority. That is the situation the Royal Castle currently finds itself in. I have filled in the missing pieces of information with my own conjectures, but I doubt they are far off the mark.”

“……Indeed. It also explains why we are currently being hunted. At the very least, we should assume that the chain of command within the Royal Castle has already been compromised.”

“――――”

“Garfiel, are you alright?”

“Huh? Y-yeah, I’m fine… Nah, honestly, it’s just a scale of trouble I never even imagined, so… I just don’t know what to say.”

Shaking his head in denial, Garfiel confesses his painfully honest feelings. However, Otto understood his junior’s feelings; it was only natural.

“……Given the situation, that is.”

Frankly speaking, Otto was equally racking his brains over the chaos and confusion. It was simply that, due to the differences in their roles within the camp, Otto was not permitted to stop thinking.

In this desperate situation, Garfiel had properly fulfilled his role. ――No, not just Garfiel. It was the result of everyone uniting as one and giving their all.

The only one who failed was the pathetic one who had his weapon taken away: himself.

“――Tch.”

Leaning his back against the wall of the room, hugging one knee as he sat, Garfiel groaned in pain from his throat.

The intense exhaustion and pain etched on his face showed no sign of fading, a state unthinkable for Garfiel, who possessed absurd toughness and recovery. This was a testament to how irregular and unreasonable the power of the one who landed a blow on him – Reinhard – truly was.

――It had been some time since Reinhard had blocked Otto and the others, and they had barely managed to break through, using every card they had.

The battle itself had lasted less than a minute, but by its end, everyone was battered and bruised. In particular, Garfiel, who had faced Reinhard head-on, was in terrible shape. Otto felt pathetic; even though he’d deliberately baited the opponent’s carelessness, a mere graze to the jaw had rendered him immobile.

The victory they had barely snatched away was only possible thanks to unexpected reinforcements. Including the fact that the situation had developed that way at all, Otto had far too much to reflect upon.

The only reason they could afford something resembling a reflection meeting was because they had been led by the arriving reinforcements and secured a temporary safe haven like this.

“……The fact that ye managed to shake him off is remarkable in itself. Even if it was a role forced upon him unwillingly, a hundred ordinary soldiers could do naught against him.”

“However, to do so, we forced her to use a card that should not have been used. What she cast away from her own life was immense. I cannot forgive that person.”

“……Your anger is more than justified. He's likely prepared to be resented. That is what it means to be the ‘Sword Saint.’ Even I have never lost my anger towards the ‘Sword Saint.’”

“That is…”

Otto quietly narrowed his eyes at the person who placed a large hand upon his own bald head.

What he had been about to say, be it a question or speculation, was swallowed back, as he realized he’d already said something he shouldn’t have.

However――

“――You must mean your anger towards my wife, not Reinhard.”

The one who took the words from the now-silent Otto, in a tone filled with certainty, was the old swordsman who opened the entrance door――Wilhelm.

Entering the room, Wilhelm was accompanied by Rem and a short-haired elderly man. He let Rem enter the room first, then turned to the man,

“Conwood, I apologize for the trouble. I am in your debt for sheltering us.”

“Hah, to think the day would come when Wilhelm Trias, the very epitome of arrogance and selfishness, would give me such an admirably grateful thanks. It might rain tomorrow.”

“You…”

“It’s a joke. ――Besides, this is only natural. It’s only natural, Wilhelm. Me lending you a hand… that’s just a matter of course, not something that requires thanks.”

“――――”

After the familiar tone, Wilhelm’s cheeks stiffened at the man whose voice trembled with emotion.

The man, seeming amused by the reaction of his old acquaintance, relaxed his cheeks. Then, looking at Otto and Garfiel inside the room,

“I owe a debt to your comrade, Natsuki Subaru, from the time of the White Whale subjugation. A debt so huge it would take a lifetime to repay. I won’t let anyone pass here, so rest easy.”

“……Master, you have our gratitude.”

“I told you. The gratitude is far greater on my side. …No one believes Natsuki Subaru-sama is part of the Witch’s Cult. It’s the same for Crusch-sama.”

With those words, the man clapped Wilhelm on the shoulder and left, closing the door behind him. Watching his back disappear behind the door, Otto called out, “Rem-san.”

This place they had arrived at under Wilhelm’s guidance was a private room in a tavern offered as a refuge. While Otto and the others were explaining their situation in this room, Rem had been in a separate room.

The reason for that was――

“Were Petra-chan and the others alright?”

“……They are resting, for now. Petra-chan was quite distraught, and Meili-chan was the one comforting her, but… they have both fallen asleep.”

“Is that so… Understood. Thank you very much.”

“No, I did nothing. More importantly, what about the discussion?”

“We’ve just finished confirming the current situation, I suppose.”

Otto replied to the tense-faced Rem, directing his light-blue eyes toward the back of the room.

Following her gaze, standing there was a large figure seated in the private room who still had his head higher than Otto or Wilhelm’s.

A bald head, a giant old frame with sun-tanned skin, his name was――

“――Barga Cromwell. One of the main figures who escalated the kingdom’s civil war in the past.”

“……Unfortunately, I don’t know who you’re talking about. I’m just Old Man Rom, a large old fart who lived in the slums, nothing more.”

“How brazen you are. What happened to the scar I gouged into your chest? Are you hiding it under that magnificent white chest hair?”

“I understand even less what you mean. Even if it’s not about me, I wouldn’t wish for old age. Seems even that famed ‘Sword Demon’ can’t match the wits of advancing years, eh?”

“You scoundrel――”

“……Both of you, please stop fighting. Petra-chan and the others are resting upstairs. We don’t have time for internal squabbling, do we?”

Stepping forward as if to wedge herself between the two glaring men, Rem glared at both in turn. At her stern gaze, Wilhelm bowed his head, and the giant figure—the old giant calling himself Old Man Rom—also cleared his throat and showed a willingness to follow Rem.

While grateful for Rem’s judgment in mediating, Otto couldn’t help but feel a certain sense of understanding toward the bitter exchange he just witnessed.

――Otto was also a citizen of this Dragonfriend Kingdom of Lugunica.

He knew the fact that ‘Sword Demon’ Wilhelm van Astrea was a hero of the ‘Demi-Human War,’ and that Barga Cromwell was one of the commanders of the Demi-Human Alliance during that civil war.

He had never imagined that Barga Cromwell was still alive.

Of course, Old Man Rom himself denied any connection to Barga, and would likely never admit it.

In any case――

“Allow me to call you Rom-san… We are grateful that you dispatched Wilhelm-san as reinforcements. Without that, we would have been annihilated by now.”

“I wouldn’t call that an exaggeration. If you’d been captured by the castle in your current state—being neither a royal selection candidate nor a knight—they could easily erase you and cover it up however they like.”

“Easily erase, that’s…”

“We must assume the worst possibility. Disliking it and escaping into optimism doesn’t mean the opponent has any reason to go easy on us. …Especially now that Miklotov is dead.”

Rem was left speechless by Old Man Rom’s words, which treated the situation gravely, but Otto agreed.

Always assume the worst possibilities. In the end, that’s what leads to finding a path to survival in a desperate situation. Even he himself thought it was pessimistic, but still.

“Hey, Wilhelm-san, ye saved my ass back there.”

At that, Garfiel, sitting near the wall, raised a hand lightly to Wilhelm. At the call, Wilhelm turned, “Garfiel-dono,” and said,

“I apologize that my skill was insufficient in that situation. Unless I took you by surprise, willing to cut you down as well, I could not land a blow on Reinhard.”

“I braced myself for that and took it, so no worries. The wound from that is already almost closed up. …The one from the ‘Sword Saint’s’ hand chop, though, is still nowhere near healed.”

“――――”

“More’n that, what were ye doin’, Wilhelm-san? I heard our boss and the Duchess over there were escapin’ together…”

“Indeed. Allow me to explain what happened on my side.”

With that, Wilhelm solemnly began to recount what had happened to him, and to his lord Crusch, up to this point.

“After Subaru-dono and Emilia-sama visited the mansion and departed, Crusch-sama, having seen them off, secluded herself in her room. Neither I nor any of the household could approach, and she hardly took any meals.”

“That… must have been worrying.”

“Indeed. Everyone understood that this could not continue. So, I sought the assistance of the former duke, Meckart Karsten-sama, Crusch-sama’s father, and was away from the mansion preparing for that. However, during that absence――”

“――Crusch-sama left the mansion alone and headed for the estate of Miklotov McMahon-dono.”

“Precisely. By the time it reached my ears, it was already too late.”

With an expression of undisguised regret, Wilhelm lamented his own inadequacy.

However, if Crusch had deliberately timed her departure for when Wilhelm was absent, it would have only been a matter of sooner or later, and there was no reason for him to be blamed.

That said, given the outcome was this situation, the ‘Sword Demon’s’ self-reproach was understandable.

“Naturally, I could not imagine Crusch-sama resorting to such a reckless act. I immediately went to the Royal Castle and appealed to an old acquaintance, Bordeaux Zellgef-dono. However, not only was I refused an ear, but I ended up being pursued by soldiers on my way back. At that point――”

“――I called out to him. Frankly, it was an agonizing choice for me.”

“……It was also not my intention to cut down Royal Kingdom soldiers and force my way through. I could not believe my eyes when I saw this man in the light of day.”

“Both of you.”

The inextinguishable anger and fated connection inevitably mixed venom into their words.

As Rem sharply scolded the two men, Otto understood the circumstances of their reunion. He also understood the process leading up to Wilhelm’s joining them.

“In that case, what about you, Rom-san? You seem to have had things remarkably well prepared, or rather, made very quick decisions.”

“It’s only natural you’d be suspicious, but I could only move just before you all as well; it’s much the same. The reason I noticed was because my nose is sharp… I’ve had a sixth sense for approaching danger since the old days. It’d gotten rusty for a while, but the recent turmoil seems to have scraped the rust off.”

“I see, is that so. ――Understood.”

Rolling his large shoulders, Old Man Rom replied matter-of-factly. Otto decided not to pry further.

Right now, they just happened to be facing the same direction; positionally, they were from opposing camps. It was natural for him to keep his cards close to his chest, and criticizing that would be narrow-minded.

At the very least, Old Man Rom’s actions had saved Otto and the others from a crisis. For now, he should prioritize evaluating those actions over doubting their true intent.

“A scary young fellow, aren’t ya. Your eyes aren’t smiling at all.”

“My apologies. A merchant’s fundamental principle is to smile outwardly while smirking inwardly, but lately, I’ve been unable to act very merchant-like. I disgust myself. ――Although, if a good-natured merchant lets his family die, then such a person is unnecessary right now.”

“――――”

“……Apologies, I spoke out of turn.”

After shrugging and replying, Otto chastised himself for those extra words.

If it was just thinking it, fine, but speaking it aloud made it a weapon. If you suddenly draw a weapon while facing someone, you can’t complain about being stabbed repeatedly.

Indeed, more than he had thought, being outmatched in his ‘Divine Protection of Soul Language’ was lingering within him. He had told himself like a curse that entrusting his identity to his Divine Protection was dangerous, yet recently he had relied on it too much. This was the price.

“――In any case, we here share the same position. Our lords have been unjustly slandered, and the Royal Castle tolerates it… no, rather, is leading the charge. Their aim is to eliminate the royal selection candidates, destroy the very rules of the royal selection, and dominate the kingdom.”

“And for that, Emilia-san, and that person too, are being spoken ill of… The ones Wilhelm-san and Rom-san support as well, is that it?”

“Emilia-sama, Felt-sama, the Duchess… so that leaves just Anastasia-sama and the church’s new candidate, Falaire-sama, huh.”

“I wonder about that. If the ‘Sages’ Council’ and the participants of the half-round table are willing to use any means, there are plenty of ways to slander Anastasia-sama. Since Anastasia-sama is from Kararagi, perhaps they’d claim she’s arranging for the city-state to invade the kingdom… or that she conspired with Emilia-sama in the Volakian Empire to assassinate Priscilla-sama――”

“――Don’t you dare jest!”

Rem raised her voice angrily at Otto’s speculation of such a malicious plot.

Her light-blue eyes moist, breathing heavily, she clenched her fists tightly, exposing her fury at the slanderous notion of using Priscilla’s death – her demise – in such a way.

“I will absolutely not allow them to slander and exploit Priscilla-san’s death. If they seriously say something like that, I will not forgive it…! If it reaches Abel-san’s ears, it will mean war with Volakia!”

“Actually, it’s not entirely a joke. Slighting Emilia-sama, who brought back the achievement of forging a friendship treaty with the Empire, is akin to throwing mud on the face of the Empire that recognized her. A ridiculous reason for war, but history is full of such ridiculous reasons. Moreover…”

“――Even if it did come to war, Reinhard is here. Controlling the Royal Castle means being able to move the ‘Sword Saint.’ It seems the authority to issue orders to the ‘Sword Saint’ was strictly managed to prevent such things until now… but the enemy has obtained it.”

“That’s… impossible…”

While it was truly the worst possible scenario, Old Man Rom did not deny Otto’s thoughts but instead paved the nightmare by filling in the gaps.

At the sheer terror of it, Rem and Garfiel, who had just barely escaped a single exchange with Reinhard with their lives, were at a loss for words.

Only one person――

“――As I thought. The ‘Divine Protection of the Sword Saint,’ is it.”

――muttered the ‘Sword Demon’ in a voice so low that almost no one could hear it.

“……Judging by the situation, it’s clear the enemy has the will to attack the royal selection. That being the case, we must assume that Falaire-sama, who recently appeared on the stage, and the ‘Divine Dragon Church’ supporting her are on the enemy’s side. To confirm, about the princess who vanished fifteen years ago…”

“――Felt is Felt. There is no other answer.”

Disliking the stagnation the silence brought to their discussion, Otto’s attempt to organize the situation and confirm facts was cut off, hard and clear, by Old Man Rom’s words.

Perhaps thinking it was too unkind to end it with just that denial over the question, Old Man Rom added “Still” to the surrounding gazes,

“That story of the ‘Divine Dragon Church’ sheltering the lost princess sounds like a tall tale to me. Even keeping a distance from the Royal Castle, to conceal that matter for over a year since the royal selection began… that’s unthinkable in a crisis threatening the kingdom’s very existence.”

Juxtaposing a firm opinion with an uncertain attitude, Old Man Rom was clearly hiding something.

Naturally, the ‘Sword Demon’s’ gaze directed at the old giant grew sharper.

“――――”

Wilhelm, who had been the captain of the Royal Guard Knights fifteen years ago at the time, was said to have been responsible for the search for the vanished princess. This time, his desire to know the answer regarding the princess suspicion cast over Felt and Falaire was likely stronger than anyone’s.

However, the mettle of the man suspected of being one of the Three Great Chiefs of the Demi-Human Alliance was not so fragile as to crack under the obsession dwelling in that sharp gaze.

In any case――

“……I understand how bad the situation is.”

Exhaling softly, Rem straightened her back firmly, seemingly forcing a shift in her feelings. Then, she looked around at the members gathered in the room—Otto and the others—in turn,

“Frankly, I’m extremely worried about that person who isn’t here right now, but Emilia-san and Sister in the castle are in danger, aren’t they? How on earth do we get them out… no, Felt-san too. How do we get them out?”

“If Reinhard and the Knight Commander are over there, a frontal assault’s just too unreasonable, no matter what. It’d be like ‘Gaddogi Guaddzeadd’s mountain retreat.’ We need a plan, Otto-nii.”

Garfiel, heavily burdened from his fight with Reinhard, agreed with Rem’s opinion and looked to Otto with eyes expecting a strategy from here on out.

For the two of them, Emilia, confined in the castle, was of course a worry, and even more so, they had to be anxious about the safety of Ram, who had accompanied her as an attendant.

Telling them this was truly painful, but――

“――No. From now on, we will prioritize escaping from the Royal Capital. We have no leeway to extract Emilia-sama and Ram-san from the Royal Castle, nor Felt-sama.”

““Wha――!?””

Eyes wide with shock, Garfiel and Rem raised their voices simultaneously. Immediately, Garfiel stood up, using the wall for support, and barked, “Otto-nii!”

“Escape… yer sayin’ we’re not goin’ to help them… what’s that supposed to mean!”

“It means exactly what I said. At present, we lack both the means and the fighting strength to extract Emilia-sama and the others imprisoned in the castle. A half-baked plan would just be crushed by brute force, and we’d all fall into enemy hands together. We cannot fight such a losing battle.”

“A losing battle… But, Sister is there, Emilia-san is…”

“I understand. However, even if the enemy has already taken control of the Royal Castle, they cannot casually lay hands on a royal selection candidate. Even Reinhard-san, who follows their orders, couldn’t overlook such a move. Their freedom will be restricted, but as long as they are in the castle, there is a high possibility that Emilia-sama and the others will not be harmed. That is my assessment.”

“B-but, still…”

Otto, striving to remain as calm as possible, carefully kept emotion from his voice, but Garfiel and Rem, their raw emotions exposed, were deeply shaken. However, into this exchange, Old Man Rom raised a large hand and interjected, “May I?”

“I agree with that young fellow. Even if they’re in the castle, I’ll manage something for Felt and the others. Rather, it’s more frightening to give those people a pretext with our movements. Their position’s already worsened because of that mabeast incident. They’d want to avoid any more.”

“Even Old Man Rom agrees with Otto-san. …What about you, Wilhelm-san?”

“――. I understand Rem-dono’s feelings of concern for her lord and sister. However, to challenge a fully prepared opponent while resigned to disadvantage is a foolish strategy… It galls me, but Barga has a point.”

Slowly shaking his head, Wilhelm answered thusly, and Rem bit her lip.

Her regret was painfully clear to Otto. Besides, there was something Otto deliberately left unsaid to avoid further backlash from her and Garfiel.

Even if the ‘Sages’ Council’ had fallen into enemy hands, they could not harm a royal selection candidate. ――However, there was no guarantee of the safety of their attendants or aides.

And that Ram, having volunteered for the role of attendant, had been prepared for that possibility from the start, which was why she didn’t yield the position to Rem or Petra.

“……Otto-nii, about leavin’ the capital… what about the boss and the others?”

“――. Meeting up would be difficult. My Divine Protection is unreliable right now. If we carelessly choose someone to talk to, our internal situation will be laid bare. We cannot risk that.”

If only his ‘Divine Protection of Soul Language’ was at its best, they could have relied on numbers to search for Subaru and the others, deliver a message, or inform them of a meeting place.

With that option gone, searching for Subaru and the others without any foothold is impossible.

“Barga, I won’t press deeply. But you should be capable of finding Crusch-sama or Subaru-dono…”

“Ye seem to think highly of a mere old fart from the slums, but unfortunately, I cannot live up to those expectations. I’m not being pretentious, nor am I holding back. The unreliable thread has already frayed. There’s no prospect of tying it back together.”

“Useless at a crucial time… No, I’m the same, aren’t I.”

He reflexively started to spit venom but hesitated, reined in by self-reflection. In Old Man Rom’s eyes, which glanced at him, there was also frustration, likely because his words were not lies.

As expected, there are no moves to make. At this situation, Rem strongly grasped the hem of her own skirt,

“The ones in the castle—Sister and the others—I can believe in. And I feel we here can work together. But that person… he’ll surely do something reckless. I just know it.”

“Rem…”

“No, I’m not the only one. Garf, Otto-san, you both know, don’t you? At times like this, that person always tries to do more than he’s capable of. And then, he’ll surely end up getting terribly hurt again. And yet…”

I can’t be by his side. No one could say anything to Rem, whose words revealed the regret she felt from her very soul.

That was surely because everyone here had been involved with Subaru in some way, had been saved by Subaru’s actions just as Rem described, and had actually witnessed him getting hurt.

“……We’ll be placing a burden on Beatrice-chan.”

Now, the only hope for the entire camp, the one who could function as a safety net for Subaru, was Beatrice, the only one likely staying with him right now. ――Just as Otto and the others thought so, “No,” Wilhelm stepped forward.

He stood before the downcast Rem, gently placing a hand on her shoulder,

“It is only natural to worry. However, Subaru-dono is not only with Beatrice-dono. Crusch-sama is there as well.”

“――. But the prevailing rumor says the Duchess has lost her mind. Indeed, did she not slip out of the mansion right under your nose?”

“Silence, Barga. What do you know of that person?”

“――――”

“You may be right that I was deceived. However, Crusch-sama must have had a reason. I will not make any assumptions until I hear it from her own lips.”

It wasn’t a tit-for-tat exchange. Wilhelm imbued his voice with a firm core, his blue eyes harboring loyalty to his absent lord as he looked at Rem, then at everyone in the room.

“Even if her memories were lost, the righteousness of her heart remains undiminished. It is not just because of a debt regarding my wife. ――I have decided, with all my soul, to seat that person upon the throne.”

“Wilhelm-san…”

“Crusch-sama is there. Subaru-dono is also a man of considerable caliber. And Beatrice-dono, though she may seem like an innocent child when with Subaru-dono, I have heard she is a Great Spirit who has lived for many long years. They will surely overcome our concerns.”

His slowly woven words were not meant to persuade Rem, but rather a forceful declaration of his hopes scribbled onto the world, commanding it to be so.

It was an assertion that felt arrogant, yet when spoken by the ‘Sword Demon’—who once defeated the ‘Sword Saint’ with his own hands and achieved a marriage that defied fate—it carried the persuasive power to make one believe. An uncanny power that made one think it might actually come true.

And that was――

“……Sounds like somethin’ the boss would say.”

“If so, that is an immensely honoring assessment.”

When Garfiel voiced what Otto himself had also felt, Wilhelm nodded deeply. Having received the ‘Sword Demon’s’ heartfelt plea up close, Rem let the tension drain from her shoulders with a soft sigh.

Her eyes and expression still held anxiety, but Rem nonetheless lifted her face with fortitude,

“I’m sorry, I became flustered. You’re right. If Beatrice-chan and Karsten-san are reliable, then his one or two reckless acts… I wonder if it will really stop at just one or two.”

“It feels like you were just about to be convinced, but isn’t it bad to get stuck on that point…?”

“Whether it’s three or four, Beatrice’ll manage somehow! …Right now, believin’ that’s all we can do, ain’t it.”

Saying that, Garfiel, still unable to shake off his own unease, hid it and clicked his fangs. Rem returned a faint, but present, smile.

Otto felt the same. No one could move in this situation having completely dispelled all anxiety. They might later regret today’s decision when an undesired outcome comes.

Even so, they had no choice but to choose, to step over the hesitation of this very moment.

“Then, once more――we will withdraw from the Royal Capital.”

Clearing his throat, Otto looked around at everyone in the room and declared this policy once again.

The Royal Castle had already fallen into enemy hands; they had become wanted fugitives targeted by the capital’s soldiers. A desperate situation where careless movement would send the ‘Sword Saint’ after them, and capture could jeopardize their very lives.

If they left the Royal Capital in such a state, it would naturally be seen as tucking tail and fleeing.

However, let it be said here and now.

“This is by no means a defeat. ――This is preparation, groundwork for a victory where we will surely hit back next time.”

“Heh! That’s just like Otto-nii, a hot-blooded declaration full’a fightin’ spirit!”

“I really can’t agree with that assessment, you know!”

Amidst the nodding faces, Otto raised his voice in response to Garfiel, who rubbed his nose with his finger. Then, after nodding to Rem, Otto directed his awareness beyond the walls—towards the Royal Capital.

He didn’t know where they were. But he thought of Subaru and Beatrice, who were likely, just like Otto and the others, floundering in a dead-end somewhere in this capital city.

The anxiety was endless. Because, just as Rem said, he would surely do something reckless.

――I don’t want to let him. That was Otto’s true feeling.

“……Even so, you’re going to do something reckless anyway, aren’t you.”

Letting the wall absorb a murmur that had no chance of reaching him, Otto pulled his hat down low over his eyes.

He knew all too well that Natsuki Subaru, for the sake of meeting someone’s expectations or wishes, would casually throw his own life and heart onto the scales.

That was why, if possible, Otto didn’t want to rely on him, and knew he shouldn’t.

Because counting Natsuki Subaru as “someone who will do something about it,” just like everyone else does, felt like preying on that kindness and weakness.

So, so at the very least.

So that his recklessness doesn’t consume Natsuki Subaru, doesn’t crush him.

Even from far away, to fight against this unreasonableness and absurdity, they must do what they themselves can. That was what Otto thought, with a bitter feeling in his heart.

　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　△▼△▼△▼△

“Achoo!”

“Did your body get cold? Are you alright, I wonder?”

“Nah, my nose just suddenly tickled. …Though, yeah, the blood really did drain from my face.”

Subaru, who sneezed from the sudden impulse attacking the back of his nose, relaxed his lips at a worried Beatrice, but couldn’t even maintain a wry smile, letting out a sigh.

Such was the impact of the story heard from Russell—the secret maneuvering of Capella of ‘Lust’ and the dire straits the Kingdom of Lugunica was in.

“It’s a given that someone with transformation powers is a pain, but… to this extent? No wonder she’s been harassing Russell-san and the others for thirty years.”

“To be precise, the harassment was directed at the Kingdom, and we were trying to stop it. Though, given our current state, we can hardly act self-important.”

“That you people were stopping it at the water’s edge is understood, I suppose. But I can’t fully accept it, I wonder. Why did this thirty-year tug-of-war suddenly tilt like this?”

“That is… probably, I think we are the reason.”

Lowering her gaze, the ‘White Sheep’ drooped her shoulders dejectedly and confessed.

Before the suspicious Subaru and the others, her eyes harboring guilt and self-reproach,

“When we ‘Beloved Children’ left and joined forces with the ‘Silver Foxes’ like this, there were many opportunities to trip up the opponent’s plans. Because of that, I think Mama also noticed. ――That the ‘Six Tongues’ had caught our tail.”

“Well, if traitors come out from your own side, it’s only natural to think that… or is it that? Capella forgets about someone the moment they leave her side, never to think of them again, sort of thing?”

“No! On the contrary, she’s the type of person who remembers it forever.”

“Thought so! Consistent interpretation there. Seriously, what a nasty piece of work, that woman…”

Once again, his understanding of Capella’s twisted personality reinforced, Subaru spat out those words. As if to supplement that exchange with the ‘White Sheep,’ Russell raised another finger,

“As she says, the enemy likely realized our hand had been strengthened. When the Witch’s Cult simultaneously attacked Priestella, the fact that ‘Lust,’ who had never shown herself before, openly revealed her presence… it’s thought she aimed to make us aware of her existence.”

“Aware of her existence… what’s the point of doing something like that…”

“――The ‘Six Tongues’ have already killed seven Capella Emerada Lugunicas.”

“Huh?”

“It’s a fact. If there was eyewitness testimony matching the physical characteristics of the ‘Lust’ confirmed in Priestella, we had no choice but to move to verify. Naturally, during that time, other schemes using the ‘Beloved Children’ were also carried out. This time’s affair is my failing for having been too divided in dealing with those.”

“……It’s probably unnecessary to ask, but those seven were fakes, I wonder?”

“Indeed. Needlessly so, as you say.”

Russell explained emotionlessly that the opponent had outmaneuvered them, remaining matter-of-fact, but if Subaru were in his position, he couldn’t imagine not being furious enough to scream ‘You’ve got to be kidding me.’

Was even that rampage in Priestella, which spawned so much tragedy, nothing more than groundwork for Capella to later toy with the ‘Six Tongues’ and seize control of the Kingdom?

After breaking and twisting the lives of so many people.

“――Tch.”

“……Subaru, I understand how you feel, but calm down, I suppose. You’re only hurting yourself, I wonder.”

“Huh? Ah, sorry. I just…”

Grinding his teeth, Subaru looked down. Beatrice, sitting in his cross-legged lap, thumped his chest with her back. What she gently touched was Subaru’s right arm, where his nails had unconsciously dug in.

Looking, he saw the burn he got at the McMahon estate, previously wrapped in a handkerchief, had been changed to clean bandages. He had unconsciously tried to dig his left nails in over the bandages again. As he was about to apologize for that unconscious act, he suddenly noticed something. ――The pain from the burn had completely vanished.

“Was this you, Russell-san… no, ‘White Sheep’-chan?”

“Eh? Ah, no, that wasn’t me. That was ‘Blue Snake’-san…”

“‘Blue Snake’?”

“――One of my subordinates. A highly skilled healer. Forgive the liberty, but while you were asleep, we provided general treatment. If there’s no discomfort…”

“Ah, yeah, none at all. So much none that it’s actually unsettling.”

He rotated his wrist lightly and swung his arm; it truly felt in perfect condition.

Even considering his mana shortage, to be able to heal a burn that Beatrice’s power could only provide first aid for… Russell’s subordinates seemed to be quite exceptional.

If his injuries were treated, Crusch’s and Racins’s should have been healed too.

Though, that said――

“――My old man.”

With a hand to his mouth, sunk in thought, Racins currently had no room for such things.

If it was true that Capella’s influence had reached the Royal Castle and that the senior nobles, starting with the ‘Sages’ Council,’ had been replaced, then Racins’ father was likely among them.

Racins, who gave off a sense of rebellion against his father with his words, yet whose unexpected intelligence glimpsed between the lines seemed to have a core certainly rooted in his upbringing. And that core was likely not unrelated to the father in question.

“Racins, you alright?”

“……I just got stripped half-naked. What’s the big deal?”

“――. I see. Got it.”

Though he probably understood the intent of the question, Subaru respected Racins’ answer.

It was only natural to be anxious. And at this very moment, Subaru had no means to resolve it, and Racins didn’t seem willing to share what was in his heart.

The feeling of worrying about one’s family is heavy. From experience, one couldn’t say talking makes it easier, so he couldn’t force it. Of course, if the other person wanted to talk, he intended to listen, but――

“――Heeey hey, has that gloomy, tedious talk finally ended?”

The door to the medical room was violently thrown open, smashing the delicate atmosphere to pieces.

The one who stomped in with the sound of presumptuous footsteps was the dangerous individual in black clothes and a harlequin mask – the ‘Black Dog,’ carrying a large bag in one hand.

Since Subaru and the others were safe, he likely was too, but,

“You sure know how to interrupt a conversation… We’re in the middle of something important.”

“Oh, my, how very busy your life must be, wonderful! Since you’re livin’ so desperately, you’d probably say there’s never a single moment you’re not havin’ an important talk, huh!”

“‘Black Dog,’ please stop it! Natsuki Subaru-san is our benefactor!”

“Ooh, actin’ all goody-goody. Even though you’re a wicked woman who’s good at makin’ others wag their tails, seems you can’t get enough waggin’ it yourself. It’s not your head but your rear that’s hangin’ low, kuhahaha!”

“Ugh…”

The ‘White Sheep,’ who had scolded ‘Black Dog’s’ rude attitude, turned red in the face at his counterattack.

It seemed these two, despite both having escaped from the ‘Beloved Children,’ didn’t share the deeply trusting relationship that Subaru and Beatrice had.

Of course, Subaru was inclined to side with the ‘White Sheep,’ but――

“You talk too much, ‘Black Dog.’ Keep it brief.”

“Tch. The preparations to move are almost ready, so all of you lords and ladies get ready too, is what I’m sayin’!”

“Garkyan, I suppose!”

“Whoa, what the!?”

Speaking roughly, ‘Black Dog’ suddenly hurled the large bag he was carrying at Subaru and the others. Subaru and Beatrice instinctively recoiled as the bag landed on the bed at their feet.

As the ‘White Sheep’ hurriedly opened the bag, its contents were――

“――Robes with a ‘Perception Inhibition’ effect. I obtained them through Roswaal. There are ones for Natsuki-dono, Beatrice-dono, and also for Crusch-sama. Ah, and a spare for Racins-dono.”

“Thanks for treating me as an afterthought!”

While Racins, treated so carelessly, spat that out, Subaru raised an eyebrow at the sound of ‘Perception Inhibition,’ which he hadn’t heard in a while, and spread the robe he took out on Beatrice’s lap.

It was white fabric. Subaru couldn’t tell just by touching it, but Beatrice nodded, “Mm,”

“Indeed, it’s undoubtedly something Roswaal had a hand in, I suppose. With this, the story of that bearded guy being Roswaal’s friend becomes more convincing, I wonder.”

“You say that like it’s unfortunate news… Well, these robes are appreciated since we’re wanted men, but did you say we’re moving? Isn’t this the ‘Six Tongues’’ hideout?”

“No, this is merely one of several small safe houses. To counter the current strength of the ‘Beloved Children,’ this is insufficient… We will vacate it promptly.”

“But that’s… No, I get that you guys, Russell-san and the others, understand the enemy’s scariness far better. We’re just hitching a ride here, sorry. I’ll follow your instructions.”

Just when they thought they had finally settled down, they were told to move again immediately. Subaru reflexively started to argue, but quickly withdrew his objection.

The enemy’s fearsomeness and meticulousness had been explained more than enough. Without having met up with Russell and his group, they would surely still be pursued by unseen enemies right now.

Therefore, Subaru decided to follow Russell’s judgment in this matter.

However――

“So, we move right away? Or rather, is the next place we’re moving to far from here?”

“Yes, it will likely take some time. ――After all, we will be leaving the Royal Capital.”

“……Eh?”

The explanation that struck his eardrums didn’t quite sink in, and Subaru’s eyes widened.

He waited, wondering if he misheard, for Russell to say different words, but his expectations were in vain; Russell’s expression remained unchanged.

Naturally, Subaru had no choice but to take time to digest those words――

“――I can’t simply nod at that, I wonder. From what you just said, it sounds like Emilia in the castle is being left behind, I suppose.”

“Yes. If I may speak without fear of misunderstanding, we also cannot spare the effort to rendezvous with your faction members who are currently fleeing the Royal Capital. We are already within the opponent’s palm. We must move before that hand closes and leaves no gaps, or it will be irrecoverable.”

“That… even so…”

“I will say it again. We will abandon this base and withdraw from the Royal Capital. Right now, this city is a den of demons controlled by the ‘Beloved Children.’ ――We cannot allow defeat.”

――At Russell’s strong determination and pride, his refusal to accept defeat, Subaru was rendered speechless.

“――――”

Subaru’s understanding is naive. Shallow. Insufficient.

The situation is even worse than Subaru imagined; they are on the verge of defeat — without realizing it, they have been placed on the executioner’s block, and the moment their heads are to be lopped off is near. That’s likely what it means.

But――

“Subaru, Subaru, look at Betty, I suppose. Betty is right here, I wonder.”

Beatrice, turning around, embraced the trembling Subaru from the front. The sensation of her small palm stroking his back reminded Subaru of how to breathe, which he had forgotten.

“I understand… Russell-san’s argument, I understand it. But, Emilia…”

Leaving the Royal Capital, which has fallen into enemy hands, refusing defeat, creating an opportunity for a comeback.

He understands the intent. He understands the logic. Right now, the Royal Capital is nothing but dangerous, and if they don’t take a decisive move, they’ll play into the enemy’s hands. ――Are they leaving Emilia behind in that place? Are they running away, giving up on reuniting with their scattered comrades?

For Natsuki Subaru, such a choice is――

“――‘White Sheep.’”

“……Y-yes.”

In front of Subaru, who was at a loss, embracing Beatrice, Russell abruptly called the ‘White Sheep.’ At his call, the ‘White Sheep’ faltered slightly, then nodded.

Then she walked up beside the bed and gently held Subaru’s hand with both of hers.

“‘White Sheep’-chan…?”

“Your feelings… I understand them so well it hurts. A decision to be separated from someone precious… it’s as agonizing as having your body torn apart. But, but still, you wouldn’t say, ‘Then let’s die together’… right?”

“――――”

“Please, believe in us. With the power of the Duchess Karsten and if Natsuki Subaru-san is here, we won’t lose, surely. I beg you… please…!”

Desperately, her eyes trembling to the point of tears, the ‘White Sheep’ persuaded Subaru.

It was an idealistic, pretty-sounding argument, a prefabricated conclusion that Subaru had repeated to himself ten times, a hundred times, to convince himself. ――And yet, somehow, hearing it from the ‘White Sheep’s’ mouth stirred his heart.

“――Russell-san. What about Emilia and the others in the castle?”

“The other side will likely refrain from laying hands on a royal selection candidate. Even if they are subjected to constraints, their personal safety should not be violated. I have collaborators watching over them.”

Taking a deep breath, exhaling, Subaru asked, and Russell answered.

The answer, which seemed to show an intent to alleviate Subaru’s anxieties as much as possible, was probably the maximum consideration and concession Russell could offer.

Emilia’s safety entrusted to the enemy’s decency, the safety of his comrades to their own strengths—considering the opponent, it was undeniably a bad gamble in many respects.

Even so――

“――I will definitely save Emilia. And everyone else too. Remember that.”

While tasting the sensation of his entire body being scorched by the black flame boiling deep in his chest, he resolved.

At Subaru’s answer, Beatrice stiffened, and the ‘White Sheep,’ still holding his hand, sighed faintly. Racins, watching silently, was given a glance by Russell. He stuck out his tongue, showing he was clearly not pleased but wouldn’t object.

Only one person, the ‘Black Dog,’ leaning his back against the wall, hand on his mask, muttered――

“――Kuhah, go die and rot, you bastard.”

――vexingly, to no one in particular. The words fell to the floor of the medicine-scented room and vanished.
